    <item>
      <title>United moves to block AI agents from its platforms, citing credential security and liability around tasks like check-in</title>
      <link>https://ai.tldr.tech/p/2026-11-12-tldr-ai</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://ai.tldr.tech/p/2026-11-12-tldr-ai</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>AI &amp; Agents</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>The restrictions cut against the grain: Expedia and Booking are partnering with agents instead. A live fight over whether travel opens up to agent traffic or walls it off.</b></p>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://ai.tldr.tech/p/2026-11-12-tldr-ai">TLDR AI</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/12%3A%20loved%20%22United%20moves%20to%20block%20AI%20agents%20from%20it...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/12%3A%20meh%20on%20%22United%20moves%20to%20block%20AI%20agents%20from%20it...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/12%3A%20less%20like%20%22United%20moves%20to%20block%20AI%20agents%20from%20it...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//ai.tldr.tech/p/2026-11-12-tldr-ai%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
